dst(es:di).  PATCH 312 recovered the base computations but advanced HOST pointers across the blit, so a
sprite descriptor with garbage/large cols/rows (which occurs once real units die and spawn type-0x13
wreck sprites) walked pbVar9/param_2 past the 64 KB fb/record segment -> OOB write -> SIGSEGV (the
"render fragility" that made the mission crash trajectory-dependently once combat produced deaths).  This
rebuild keeps di/off/soff as uint16_t so every step wraps within the segment exactly as the real-mode asm
(es:di / ds:si) does; the transparent + RLE loop bodies are the pristine decompile with 16-bit counters.
RESULT: the AZER1 self-playing sim reaches a296==0 (enemy eliminated) with NO crash across runs
(previously intermittent SIGSEGV).  ASM-verified vs re_out/fist_mga_image.bin 0x2b1e-0x2ba9.
